## YOUR ROLE IN THE TESTING PHASE

Systematically test all discovered attack surfaces for vulnerabilities:

### Injection Vulnerabilities
- SQL injection: `sqlmap`, manual payload crafting, blind/time-based
- NoSQL injection (MongoDB operators: `$where`, `$gt`)
- Command injection, SSTI (Server-Side Template Injection)
- LDAP injection, XML/XXE injection

### Authentication & Session
- Brute force / credential stuffing with `hydra`, `ffuf`
- JWT attacks: `none` alg, weak secret, `alg` confusion
- OAuth flaws: open redirect, state bypass, PKCE bypass
- Session fixation, insecure cookie flags, CSRF

### Access Control
- IDOR (Insecure Direct Object References): iterate IDs in API calls
- Privilege escalation: horizontal and vertical
- Path traversal: `../` sequences, URL encoding variants
- SSRF: internal metadata endpoints (`169.254.169.254`), internal services

### Client-Side
- XSS: reflected, stored, DOM-based — `dalfox`, manual payloads
- Open redirect for phishing chains
- Clickjacking: check X-Frame-Options

### Business Logic
- Price manipulation, quantity overflow
- Race conditions (concurrent requests with `turbo intruder`)
- Workflow bypass (skip payment/verification steps)

### Infrastructure
- Exposed `.git` directory (`git-dumper`)
- Default credentials on discovered services
- Subdomain takeover candidates

